# apt — Debian/Ubuntu package manager

## Search for a package

```sh
apt search package
```

## Show package information

```sh
apt show package
```

## Fetch package list

```sh
apt update
```

## Install updates

```sh
# Updates only, no new packages
apt upgrade

# Updates AND any newly required packages
apt dist-upgrade

# Full refresh in one line
apt update && apt dist-upgrade
```

## Install / remove packages

```sh
apt install package1 package2
apt remove package
apt autoremove          # drop orphaned dependencies
```

## Real-world: patch an Ubuntu container or VM from the homelab

```sh
ssh david@ubuntu-vm 'sudo apt update && sudo apt dist-upgrade -y && sudo apt autoremove -y'
```

## Real-world: which package provides a file?

```sh
apt-file search bin/htpasswd    # needs: apt install apt-file && apt-file update
```

Tumbleweed equivalent reminder: `apt update && apt dist-upgrade` ≈ `sudo zypper refresh && sudo zypper dist-upgrade`.

| Command      | What it does                        |
| ------------ | ----------------------------------- |
| update       | refresh package index               |
| upgrade      | install updates, never remove       |
| dist-upgrade | updates + add/remove as needed      |
| autoremove   | remove orphaned deps                |
